# ============================================================================
# Morse Torch: say it, flash it, read it back.
#
#   Type a message or press "Say it" and speak. "Send" flashes it in Morse on
#   the torch. "Watch for light" finds whatever is flashing in the camera's
#   picture, writes the letters as they come, and reads the message out when
#   the light goes quiet. Send while watching and a mirror will show you both
#   halves at once.
#
#   What it uses, all through Vml(...):
#     Listen      speech to text          Flash        a timed on/off pattern
#     WatchLight  "the light went on/off, and how long the last state lasted"
#     Speak       text to speech          Torch        just a torch
#   In a browser Flash lights the whole screen, which a phone reads as well.
#
#   The Morse itself is the Lua at the bottom: Pattern() turns text into
#   milliseconds on and off, and Read() turns flashes back into text.
#
#   Made with Visualised.
# ============================================================================

@Window MorseTorch
Title=Morse Torch
Version=1.1
Icon=MorseTorch.png
Width=360
Height=640
OnOpened=Start

@MenuTheme theme
Parent=MorseTorch
Background=#111827

@Canvas c
Parent=MorseTorch
Background=#FFFFFF

@TextBlock lblTitle
Parent=c
Canvas.Left=12
Canvas.Top=8
Width=336
Height=28
FontSize=20
FontWeight=Bold
Text=Morse Torch

# --- sending: the message, and how fast ---------------------------------------

@TextBox txtSay
Parent=c
Canvas.Left=12
Canvas.Top=42
Width=336
Height=64
AcceptsReturn=true
TextWrapping=Wrap
Watermark=Type a message, or press Say it
Text=SOS
Anchor=Top,Left,Right

@Button btnSay
Parent=c
Canvas.Left=12
Canvas.Top=114
Width=106
Height=40
Content=Say it
OnClick=DoSay

@Button btnSend
Parent=c
Canvas.Left=127
Canvas.Top=114
Width=106
Height=40
